WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:02.110
In the present time,

00:02.660 --> 00:05.980
With VR headgear,
you can go into a virtual world

00:05.980 --> 00:09.570
and play as the resident of that world.

00:09.570 --> 00:13.790
VR Full-Dive games are
at the height of their popularity.

00:14.970 --> 00:17.970
And there exists

00:17.970 --> 00:21.960
a god-tier game that stands
above all other games

00:21.960 --> 00:24.630
with over thirty million
players worldwide.

00:24.630 --> 00:26.380
And the name of that game is...

00:26.880 --> 00:29.280
Shangri-La Frontier.

00:50.150 --> 00:56.120
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

02:07.980 --> 02:12.110
F... Found you!

02:12.110 --> 02:14.240
Wh-What?!

02:15.870 --> 02:18.870
Emul!

02:21.120 --> 02:21.700
Emul!

02:21.700 --> 02:25.040
#28: ACCELERATING CONFERENCE, SURGING GREED,
Emul!

02:25.040 --> 02:26.630
AND MULTIPLE BEGINNINGS
Emul!

02:26.630 --> 02:29.630
Hell no! They're completely berserk!

02:30.090 --> 02:32.050
Let's go, guys!

02:33.800 --> 02:36.550
You bastards...!

02:36.550 --> 02:38.680
You two sold me off, didn't you?!

02:38.680 --> 02:40.470
Now we're even.

02:40.470 --> 02:41.680
Dammit!

02:50.860 --> 02:54.320
Mr. Sunraku! We're done!

02:54.320 --> 02:55.700
No, wait...

02:57.160 --> 02:58.200
Isn't she...

03:01.620 --> 03:04.210
That means... their target is...

03:08.170 --> 03:09.500
...not me!

03:21.710 --> 03:24.640
Mr. Sunraku!
How could you betray me!

03:28.230 --> 03:30.190
Don't hate me, Emul.

03:30.190 --> 03:32.570
Sometimes sacrifice is a must.

03:32.570 --> 03:36.030
It's like a horde of zombies
feasting on fresh meat.

03:36.030 --> 03:40.910
It's a pain to calm Animalia down
without Emul around, after all.

03:40.910 --> 03:43.290
Hold on, why did you
even call these guys fo...

03:43.290 --> 03:45.910
What's with all the urgency, Pencilgon?

03:51.320 --> 03:52.920
Hey there, Momo!

03:54.960 --> 03:56.220
Psyger-0!

03:57.720 --> 04:00.470
I've been wanting to talk
to you for a while.

04:00.470 --> 04:01.990
Sunraku.

04:02.840 --> 04:07.930
I'm Psyger-100,
the leader of the Clan Schwarz Vulf.

04:08.550 --> 04:10.060
And this is Psyger-0.

04:14.780 --> 04:16.530
Um, hi.

04:17.070 --> 04:18.910
Oh, hi.

04:21.000 --> 04:22.700
Hizutome!

04:22.700 --> 04:28.120
He somehow looks even stronger
and cooler than the last time I saw him!

04:28.120 --> 04:29.710
JUST HER IMAGINATION

04:30.500 --> 04:34.590
Is it just me or they're looking at me
more intensely than before?

04:35.510 --> 04:39.430
Oh, I see you like it sized
down by a lot like always.

04:40.590 --> 04:43.890
Shut up! Stop pointing
that out each time we meet!

04:44.930 --> 04:46.640
Do they know each other in real life?

04:46.640 --> 04:49.310
Anyway, are you sure about this?

04:49.310 --> 04:52.270
As you asked me,
I did reach out to him.

04:52.270 --> 04:58.650
Well, well. I never would've thought
you'd contact me instead.

04:58.650 --> 05:01.910
I'm far too old to run,
but I sprinted here anyway.

05:02.370 --> 05:04.370
You're from that lore clan...

05:04.990 --> 05:06.450
It's "Professor," if you please.

05:06.450 --> 05:09.250
Thank you for earlier, Sunraku.

05:09.250 --> 05:12.120
Whoa, Pencilgon.
What's the meaning of this?

05:12.120 --> 05:14.460
We're not here just to
stand around, aren't we?

05:14.460 --> 05:17.880
I reserved a room at
the Crystal City Serpent's Apple for us.

05:17.880 --> 05:19.880
We can talk over there.

05:19.880 --> 05:24.640
SERPENT'S APPLE

05:31.140 --> 05:35.020
SCHWARZ VULF LEADER
PSYGER-100

05:35.020 --> 05:38.030
PSYGER-0

05:38.030 --> 05:41.530
SF-ZOO LEADER
ANIMALIA

05:41.530 --> 05:45.030
LIBRARY LEADER
PROFESSOR

05:45.030 --> 05:46.950
OIKATZO

05:46.950 --> 05:48.790
SUNRAKU

05:48.790 --> 05:51.160
WOLF-GANG LEADER
ARTHUR PENCILGON

05:57.670 --> 06:00.340
Okay, okay, I see it now.

06:00.340 --> 06:03.720
So you want me to answer all
your questions in one go, eh?

06:03.720 --> 06:04.970
What a pain.

06:04.970 --> 06:07.760
I wanna go home already.

06:07.760 --> 06:13.000
You're the only one who can answer
Schwarz Vulf and SF-Zoo's requests.

06:13.000 --> 06:15.690
You don't want them
to keep stalking you, do you?

06:18.020 --> 06:19.570
All right, fine.

06:20.320 --> 06:22.490
Now, let's get this started, shall we?

06:23.530 --> 06:26.990
We have so many notable figures
right here, all in one place.

06:26.990 --> 06:28.990
Let's make a good time of this.

06:31.160 --> 06:34.000
Let me just cut straight
to the point here, then.

06:34.750 --> 06:39.000
What we in Schwarz Vulf want is
information on the unique monster,

06:39.000 --> 06:41.260
Lycagon the Nightslayer.

06:41.260 --> 06:43.130
In exchange...

06:43.880 --> 06:48.620
We'll provide you with a means
of removing that Lycagon's Mark.

06:49.600 --> 06:50.640
For real?!

06:50.640 --> 06:53.600
The method itself is fairly well-known.

06:53.600 --> 06:58.440
But with our help, you can get it done
times easier than doing it from scratch.

06:59.690 --> 07:01.940
You can remove this Mark?

07:01.940 --> 07:05.950
This helped me a bit, but being
able to equip stuff is a big deal!

07:06.490 --> 07:11.580
Schwarz Vulf's final goal is to defeat
Lycagon the Nightslayer.

07:12.000 --> 07:17.640
But regrettably, we have yet to properly
take on a unique monster before.

07:18.330 --> 07:21.000
Even when we were lucky enough
to run into Lycagon,

07:21.000 --> 07:24.470
we'd just get destroyed
without learning anything useful.

07:26.220 --> 07:29.220
Now then, how much should I tell them?

07:29.220 --> 07:35.480
The Vorpal Epic, the EX Unique Scenario
I have exclusive access to...

07:36.140 --> 07:41.150
Telling them about Rabitz, Vysache,
and the rabbits from the palace,

07:41.150 --> 07:43.940
as well as Aramis,
is out of the question.

07:44.530 --> 07:47.530
If the SF-Zoo Clan finds out about it...

07:47.530 --> 07:52.160
I'll undoubtedly see no more
days of peace in SLF.

07:54.160 --> 07:55.370
I wanna go home.

07:55.370 --> 07:57.460
I can't let my guard down
on these two, either.

07:57.460 --> 08:01.210
They already know about
Bilac and Aramis, after all.

08:01.210 --> 08:02.920
Especially Pencilgon.

08:04.630 --> 08:05.720
What?

08:05.720 --> 08:08.090
Smitten by my beauty?

08:08.090 --> 08:09.340
Tell yourself that.

08:10.220 --> 08:15.020
If she gets even a sniff on this,
she'll surely pursue it like a police dog.

08:16.600 --> 08:22.060
The only thing I can talk about here
is about Wethermon and Lycagon.

08:22.770 --> 08:27.610
I'll use that as a cover and keep
my knowledge of Rabitz a secret!

08:27.610 --> 08:29.950
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

08:29.950 --> 08:30.990
SERPENT'S APPLE

08:30.990 --> 08:33.450
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON
SERPENT'S APPLE

08:42.210 --> 08:47.260
I think you can't defeat a unique monster
by simply fighting them.

08:50.490 --> 08:54.160
For example, Wethermon the Tombguard
that we defeated...

08:54.970 --> 09:00.730
To challenge him, we had to take
a specific EX Unique Scenario.

09:01.850 --> 09:03.150
Right.

09:03.150 --> 09:06.940
Unique monsters form the core
of EX Unique Scenario.

09:06.940 --> 09:08.360
Lycagon the Nightslayer

09:08.360 --> 09:09.110
RANDOM ENCOUNTER:
is a random encounter.

09:09.110 --> 09:10.700
CAN BE ENCOUNTERED RANDOMLY ON THE FIELD
is a random encounter.

09:10.700 --> 09:12.950
So although you "can" fight it,

09:12.950 --> 09:18.160
chances are you need to flip some scenario
flags before you can actually defeat it.

09:19.040 --> 09:25.000
And those flags are likely hidden in
the newly added continent with the big update.

09:25.000 --> 09:27.420
Well, I can't say that for sure,

09:27.420 --> 09:34.970
but I think they'll be connected to
the two unique monsters yet to be discovered.

09:37.970 --> 09:40.180
Speaking of the new continent...

09:40.180 --> 09:45.820
I hope my wife isn't bothering you,
Psyger-100.

09:46.300 --> 09:49.510
Oh, you mean Ms. Massive Dynamite?

09:49.510 --> 09:51.510
Yeah, she was super excited.

09:52.280 --> 09:53.490
I see.

09:53.490 --> 09:56.950
She must've been looking forward
to going to the new continent.

09:56.950 --> 09:57.910
Good grief...

09:57.910 --> 09:59.040
It's a bit embarrassing

09:59.040 --> 10:01.120
- Wife?
- hearing her not acting her age.

10:01.120 --> 10:02.460
- What kinda relationship do they have?
- Her spirit for exploration

10:02.460 --> 10:03.790
- What kinda relationship do they have?
- is something worth admiring.

10:04.780 --> 10:05.790
Now then.

10:06.460 --> 10:13.550
Let's do a rundown on the Seven Colossi
that we do know about.

10:13.550 --> 10:16.010
First, Lycagon the Nightslayer.

10:16.010 --> 10:18.810
A black wolf encountered randomly.

10:18.810 --> 10:21.230
LYCAGON THE NIGHTSLAYER
The word says she's actually female.

10:21.640 --> 10:23.230
Second, Ctarnidd of the Abyss.

10:23.230 --> 10:23.850
CTARNIDD OF THE ABYSS
Second, Ctarnidd of the Abyss.

10:23.850 --> 10:25.400
CTARNIDD OF THE ABYSS
A unique monster that appears

10:25.400 --> 10:26.230
CTARNIDD OF THE ABYSS
in the ocean with the shape of an octopus.

10:26.230 --> 10:28.270
in the ocean with the shape of an octopus.

10:28.270 --> 10:32.070
However, no player has actually
seen it in person.

10:32.070 --> 10:36.240
All our info about it comes
from half-crazed NPCs.

10:36.780 --> 10:38.240
Siegwurm the Sky Ruler.

10:38.240 --> 10:38.950
SIEGWURM THE SKY RULER
Siegwurm the Sky Ruler.

10:38.950 --> 10:41.250
SIEGWURM THE SKY RULER
A golden dragon encountered randomly.

10:41.250 --> 10:42.330
A golden dragon encountered randomly.

10:42.330 --> 10:43.750
Just like Lycagon,

10:43.750 --> 10:47.880
you can encounter it randomly,
so many have actually seen it.

10:47.880 --> 10:51.260
But it flies too high up to fight.

10:52.090 --> 10:56.340
It's said to be fightable in
the Magnanimous Sanctuary area,

10:56.340 --> 10:59.760
where it constantly seeks those
brave enough to challenge it.

11:03.770 --> 11:05.810
Orchestra of the Doom Echo.

11:05.810 --> 11:07.020
ORCHESTRA OF THE DOOM ECHO
Orchestra of the Doom Echo.

11:07.020 --> 11:08.520
ORCHESTRA OF THE DOOM ECHO
Its existence was discovered

11:08.520 --> 11:12.390
in a book by a player who raided

11:12.390 --> 11:18.280
the royal library of Ainverth,
the kingdom ruling over this entire region.

11:18.790 --> 11:25.620
It's said to control tsunamis, clad in fire,
and can summon lightning.

11:25.620 --> 11:28.210
But outside of its name,
nothing else is known.

11:29.500 --> 11:35.470
And the fifth is Wethermon the Tombguard
that Sunraku and his friends defeated.

11:38.720 --> 11:41.430
Why are you trying to run on me?

11:41.430 --> 11:44.850
U-Ugh, I'm not needed here, right?!

11:44.850 --> 11:46.560
O-Ouch, let go of me!

11:46.560 --> 11:51.360
We in the Library have done
a lot of research,

11:51.360 --> 11:56.780
but truth be told, we don't have
any non-public info on him.

11:56.780 --> 11:58.240
Well, well.

11:59.200 --> 12:01.450
I do have an item for you!

12:02.830 --> 12:04.290
Ta-dah!

12:04.290 --> 12:07.330
The Tomb of Truth: The Tombguard!

12:09.330 --> 12:11.170
WHAT?!

12:11.170 --> 12:13.460
SECRET
It's packed to the brim

12:13.460 --> 12:15.300
SECRET
with valuable info on Wethermon!

12:15.300 --> 12:17.090
SECRET
Wh-What!

12:19.010 --> 12:24.390
It's an incredibly rare item that
I normally would never let go of,

12:24.390 --> 12:29.310
but if it's someone like you,
one who knows how valuable this book is...

12:30.980 --> 12:36.070
Depending on your "sincerity,"
I might give it to you. What do you say?

12:36.070 --> 12:37.190
SINCERITY = MONEY

12:37.190 --> 12:38.570
Yes, please!

12:38.570 --> 12:41.070
I'll pay whatever you want!

12:41.070 --> 12:42.740
- By the way, the market price
- Yeah, right.

12:42.740 --> 12:44.410
- is about this much.
- Those tombs are pretty much worthless

12:44.410 --> 12:46.080
- Will that be okay with you?
- after you read them two or three times.

12:46.080 --> 12:47.370
- What?!
- She's taking him for everything he's got.

12:47.370 --> 12:49.500
- But considering the value of this book,
- She's taking him for everything he's got.

12:49.500 --> 12:51.500
- I believe this is the right price.
- As you can see, we're starving for info.

12:51.500 --> 12:52.960
- As you can see, we're starving for info.

12:53.840 --> 12:55.210
And Sunraku.

12:56.210 --> 12:59.800
You're the only one who has
information on Lycagon the Nightslayer.

13:01.510 --> 13:03.800
I don't know a whole lot myself.

13:04.230 --> 13:05.430
That's fine.

13:05.430 --> 13:08.600
Even knowing her basic
action pattern would be great.

13:09.040 --> 13:10.350
Okay.

13:10.350 --> 13:12.100
In that case...

13:12.750 --> 13:14.610
First, her physical attacks.

13:14.610 --> 13:16.360
There are only a few tells,

13:16.360 --> 13:19.780
and they came faster than most bosses,
but you can still parry them.

13:20.520 --> 13:25.290
Her swipes typically come in three patterns;
diagonal, vertical, and horizontal.

13:25.290 --> 13:27.950
She uses a lot of delays as well,

13:27.950 --> 13:30.910
but there are surprisingly
a lot of safe zones.

13:31.320 --> 13:35.340
I'll get into details later,
but her bite attacks are a headache.

13:35.960 --> 13:39.340
She didn't use them much on me,
but they have the "destruction" attribute.

13:39.340 --> 13:43.260
In fact, I think most of her
physical attacks have that by default.

13:43.840 --> 13:46.740
Anyway, one bite will
easily rip you apart.

13:46.740 --> 13:49.850
As for her AOE attack that turns
her shadows into spears...

13:49.850 --> 13:51.520
W-Wait a minute.

13:51.520 --> 13:52.600
Huh?

13:52.600 --> 13:57.560
I was led to believe you
only faced Lycagon once.

13:57.560 --> 14:02.450
But you analyzed her to that level
on your first fight against her?

14:02.450 --> 14:04.530
Against that Lycagon the Nightslayer...

14:05.350 --> 14:07.530
This guy's a freak.

14:07.530 --> 14:10.040
Yup, a complete freak, I tell you.

14:10.040 --> 14:12.710
What's that supposed to mean?!

14:12.710 --> 14:15.920
And you dress like that
because you like it, don't you?

14:15.920 --> 14:17.290
I know, right!

14:17.290 --> 14:21.420
A-A freak? So that means...!

14:21.420 --> 14:24.680
After hearing that he's
hanging out with Pencilgon,

14:24.680 --> 14:27.630
I was wondering
what kind of person he is.

14:28.180 --> 14:29.810
But I see.

14:30.600 --> 14:32.640
Sunraku...

14:33.140 --> 14:36.190
Something tells me you will
trigger big things in the future.

14:37.730 --> 14:39.890
Sorry. You can keep going.

14:39.890 --> 14:42.440
I'd appreciate it if you could
write them down for me later.

14:42.440 --> 14:44.280
Fine.

14:44.280 --> 14:48.450
Well, for the most part,
it's more or less like fighting a giant wolf.

14:49.080 --> 14:52.250
But I do have some things
that I don't understand.

14:52.250 --> 14:53.460
What do you mean?

14:56.630 --> 14:59.750
The last attack that Lycagon
the Nightslayer hit me with...

14:59.750 --> 15:01.920
What did she just do to me?

15:03.090 --> 15:04.170
What did she hit me with?

15:05.430 --> 15:08.580
I'm pretty sure I could've dodged
anything she could throw at me.

15:09.180 --> 15:12.310
Or more like, I should've been
outside of her range of attack.

15:13.270 --> 15:16.270
At first, I thought maybe it was
an unavoidable area attack,

15:16.270 --> 15:17.920
but it didn't seem like it.

15:18.940 --> 15:23.570
System-wise, monsters don't suddenly
appear out of nowhere in this game, right?

15:23.570 --> 15:25.530
No, it's not set up that way.

15:28.620 --> 15:29.950
I'll bet.

15:29.950 --> 15:31.990
This isn't some trash game.

15:31.990 --> 15:34.080
With all the details
they put into this world,

15:34.080 --> 15:37.960
I doubt they would deploy an important
unique monster in such a sloppy way.

15:38.790 --> 15:40.460
In that case...

15:40.460 --> 15:43.670
You think it's some kind of ability
on Lycagon's part?

15:49.220 --> 15:52.850
I also don't have that much
information on Lycagon.

15:53.300 --> 15:56.560
If I could fight her again,
maybe I could grasp more, but...

15:59.960 --> 16:01.020
I see.

16:03.440 --> 16:05.030
Interesting!

16:06.900 --> 16:09.780
That should be enough info from me.

16:09.780 --> 16:12.580
I managed to get through without
mentioning Rabitz for now.

16:14.950 --> 16:17.040
By the way.

16:17.040 --> 16:20.040
Sunraku, Pencilgon, OiKatzo.

16:20.750 --> 16:24.880
The name of your Clan
was "Wolf-Gang," right?

16:24.880 --> 16:25.880
What do you say?

16:25.880 --> 16:27.670
Want to form an alliance with us as...

16:27.670 --> 16:29.550
Hold on, Schwarz Vulf.

16:30.000 --> 16:33.100
Can you hold on to
that proposal for later?

16:34.930 --> 16:38.480
That wasn't part of your
original question, was it?

16:38.480 --> 16:40.230
Well, yeah.

16:40.750 --> 16:44.320
And I got to discuss this with
that person first about this.

16:46.320 --> 16:48.530
Now it's my turn.

16:48.530 --> 16:52.400
We in SF-Zoo only have one question.

16:57.370 --> 17:02.210
About Rabitz,
the land of Vorpal Bunnies!

17:03.920 --> 17:06.380
And by the name of SF-Zoo,

17:06.380 --> 17:10.260
I'm gonna squeeze all I can
get from you, Mr. Sunraku.

17:10.260 --> 17:14.390
Tch, I knew you would do this, Animalia!

17:14.390 --> 17:19.520
I'm sure she wants to ask about
the Rabitz-related unique scenario.

17:23.310 --> 17:26.070
Yes, what I want to know the most...

17:33.120 --> 17:37.120
...is a free pass to Rabitz,
the land of rabbits!

17:37.700 --> 17:38.410
Huh?

17:40.160 --> 17:40.910
Huh?

17:43.500 --> 17:45.160
A free pass?

17:45.160 --> 17:45.840
That's right!

17:46.420 --> 17:51.840
Everyone knows that you can go there
with the unique scenario, Tour of Rabitz.

17:52.360 --> 17:57.140
But if you defeated Lagonian Python,
the snake attacking the land,

17:57.140 --> 18:02.600
you'll be forced out of Rabitz
and never allowed to come back!

18:03.770 --> 18:05.230
And yet...!

18:05.750 --> 18:10.650
Mr. Sunraku, not only did you bring this
talking Vorpal Bunny out of the land,

18:10.650 --> 18:14.280
you're supposedly going in and out
of Rabitz all the time!

18:14.280 --> 18:16.410
I want to know how to do it.

18:16.410 --> 18:22.500
If you tell me, we will offer you
anything we can in return!

18:26.540 --> 18:29.550
Here I was thinking she'd ask me
to reveal the unique scenario

18:29.550 --> 18:32.130
needed to make Emul a party member.

18:32.130 --> 18:33.880
But maybe I can do something about this?

18:34.510 --> 18:36.390
Umm...

18:36.930 --> 18:40.180
The Invitation from Rabitz
that I triggered...

18:40.180 --> 18:43.390
I can't exactly reveal this to them...

18:43.390 --> 18:46.770
If that's what you want,
it'd be faster to just ask Emul about it,

18:46.770 --> 18:48.520
so I'd like you to give her back.

18:51.440 --> 18:53.700
Fine, if I have to...

18:54.610 --> 18:55.760
Hey.

18:56.850 --> 18:59.280
Hey, come back for me.

18:59.730 --> 19:00.660
No luck.

19:01.200 --> 19:02.700
She's limp.

19:05.050 --> 19:08.210
All-you-eat special Rabitz parfaits.

19:08.210 --> 19:09.920
It's my treat.

19:13.590 --> 19:16.000
Special Rabitz parfaits?!

19:16.680 --> 19:17.930
Where?!

19:17.930 --> 19:19.850
And it's your treat, Mr. Sunraku?!

19:19.850 --> 19:21.310
Okay, she's back.

19:23.350 --> 19:26.600
Huh? What was I doing?

19:26.600 --> 19:27.560
So cute!

19:27.980 --> 19:29.520
For whatever reason,

19:29.520 --> 19:33.360
all I can remember was that Mr. Sunraku
would buy me special Rabitz parfaits

19:33.360 --> 19:35.610
and this spellbook that I wanted.

19:35.610 --> 19:36.570
Don't pad it!

19:36.570 --> 19:39.530
More importantly,
I've got a question to ask.

19:39.530 --> 19:40.530
What is it?

19:40.990 --> 19:42.950
It's about Rabitz.

19:42.950 --> 19:44.910
Sometimes you guys
invite players, um,

19:44.910 --> 19:47.790
Adventurers to beat up
some snakes for you, right?

19:47.790 --> 19:48.670
Yes.

19:48.670 --> 19:53.370
That means it's not like humans
aren't allowed to be there, right?

19:54.590 --> 19:57.010
Yes, I don't think so.

19:57.010 --> 20:01.220
Is there a way for those who leave
to come back to Rabitz, then?

20:03.640 --> 20:08.730
That's kind of a government issue,
so I can't give a clear answer to that.

20:09.230 --> 20:13.650
But Brother Aydward is
a really brainy, creative kinda guy.

20:13.650 --> 20:16.610
I'm sure he'll lend a hand
if you're asking!

20:16.610 --> 20:19.030
Another new rabbit?

20:19.030 --> 20:21.370
He's my eldest brother!

20:21.370 --> 20:24.370
He's the king of Rabitz!

20:24.370 --> 20:24.870
A king?

20:24.870 --> 20:26.430
That's right!

20:30.290 --> 20:33.710
So Vash wasn't the one ruling Rabitz?

20:33.710 --> 20:36.760
Does that mean he already retired
and gave the throne to his son?

20:37.340 --> 20:39.680
Could you ask him now?

20:39.680 --> 20:41.510
O-Of course!

20:41.510 --> 20:47.540
I'll hop right on over
and go in-depth about this with him!

20:48.190 --> 20:49.560
Thank you!

20:49.560 --> 20:52.060
A-Aah! Emul!

20:52.490 --> 20:56.360
She quite literally fled from us.
Hopping while at it.

20:57.780 --> 21:00.570
I wanted to muffle her fur one last time.

21:01.100 --> 21:05.080
Can we save this topic for later
when Emul returns?

21:07.500 --> 21:08.830
I guess we have to.

21:11.170 --> 21:12.830
So be it.

21:15.960 --> 21:17.760
Let's go with that price.

21:18.590 --> 21:21.130
All right! We have a deal!

21:21.130 --> 21:23.970
Hurry! Let me read it already!

21:23.970 --> 21:27.100
Here you go!
The Tomb of Truth: The Tombguard.

21:30.140 --> 21:32.650
How much did you fleece him for?

21:32.650 --> 21:34.060
100 million mahni!

21:34.060 --> 21:35.900
That's nasty.

21:35.900 --> 21:38.610
It's still only cover
20% of my dept, though.

21:39.530 --> 21:44.200
Well then, may I make my request now?

21:44.200 --> 21:46.830
It's for Schwarz Vulf,

21:47.830 --> 21:48.790
Library,

21:49.910 --> 21:50.830
SF-Zoo,

21:52.130 --> 21:54.460
and us in Wolf-Gang.

21:57.090 --> 21:58.960
I'd like us to form a Clan Alliance.
